<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Stuart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1371">1371</a>–<a href="/years/1714">1714</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as House of Stewart, Stuart dynasty, Stuarts, Stewart dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Stuart was a royal dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> from 1371 and, from the accession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i">James VI and I</a> in 1603, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Ireland as well. Its reigns saw the Plantation of Ulster, the civil wars and the execution of Charles I in 1649, the Restoration and the Glorious Revolution of 1688, which removed James II. The dynasty's rule ended with the death of Queen Anne in 1714.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-stuart.jpg" alt="House of Stuart" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_England_(1603%E2%80%931649).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
